From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: babarot <b4b4r07@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:09:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Edit Markdown files in place with a CodeMirror editor

An edit button next to the ToC and raw toggles swaps the rendered view
for a CodeMirror editor that fills the content area. Saving writes the
file on disk, or replaces the content of an uploaded file, through a new
PUT on the file's content endpoint. The editor saves on Cmd/Ctrl+S, when
it closes and when another file is selected, and after a second of
inactivity when auto save is on.

Switching between the view and the editor keeps the place: the nearest
heading above the cursor or the top of the viewport is found on the
other side, falling back to the scroll ratio.

The settings dialog gains an Editor section: a color scheme, applied to
the editor's syntax highlighting, line wrapping and auto save.
